solution:
To find the number of prime divisors of $30!$, we identify all prime numbers $p$ such that $p \le 30$. Since $30!$ is the product of integers from 1 to 30, any prime less than or equal to 30 appears as a factor. No prime greater than 30 can divide $30!$ because it would require a factor larger than 30.

The primes less than or equal to 30 are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23, and 29. Counting these yields four single-digit primes, four primes in the teens, and two primes in the twenties. Summing these groups ($4 + 4 + 2$) gives a total of 10 distinct prime divisors. Thus, there are exactly 10 positive divisors of $30!$ that are prime.

\boxed{10}

